- (1) The K -hop neighborhoods of u and v do not overlap, i.e., ( ⋃ 0 ≤ k ≤ K N k u ) ∩ ( ⋃ 0 ≤ k ≤ K N k v ) = ∅ ;
- (2) For any node w ∈ N k v (where 0 ≤ k ≤ K -1 ), there exists an edge ( w,w ∗ ) ∈ E where w ∗ ∈ N k +1 v and w ∗ does not connect any node in N k v other than w ; Similar constraint applies to node u 's neighborhood N k u ;
- (3) The structures (i.e., not considering node features) of the K -hop neighborhood of u and v are isomorphic. i.e., For the two subgraphs induced by ⋃ 0 ≤ k ≤ K N k v and ⋃ 0 ≤ k ≤ K N k u , we can find an isomorphic node mapping F where F ( u ) = v , and a node v ′ ∈ N k v is mapped by F to a node u ′ ∈ N k u .
